  "body": "## What changed\nFour more Tormach machine files, each built from its own operator's manual. They follow the pattern from #259.\n\n| File | Machine | Manual | Spindle (belts) | Rapid = feed ceiling |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `tormach-pcnc770-s3.mch` | PCNC 770 (Series 3) | 32426 Rev C1-1 (2011), p. 9-2 | 175–10200 rpm (175–3250 / 525–10200) | X/Y 135, Z 100 IPM |\n| `tormach-pcnc1100-s1.mch` | PCNC 1100 (Series I) | 30625 Rev C4-1 (2008), p. 9-2 | 300–4500 rpm (300–1750 / 800–4500) | 65 IPM on all axes |\n| `tormach-pcnc1100-s2.mch` | PCNC 1100 (Series II) | 31138 Rev B1-4, p. 9-2 | 100–5140 rpm (100–2000 / 250–5140) | X/Y 90, Z 65 IPM |\n| `tormach-pcnc1100-s3.mch` | PCNC 1100 (Series 3) | UM10087 1013A (2013), p. 121 | 100–5140 rpm (100–2000 / 250–5140) | X/Y 110, Z 90 IPM |\n\n- **Common to all four:** inch, R8 spindle, coolant M7 mist / M8 flood, and `rigid_tapping: false`. These manuals tap with tapping-head macros (M871–M874), so the Tormach post refuses G84 by name on these machines, as it already does on the 770M and PCNC 440.\n- **Spindle power** is the continuous rating, not the peak, as in the PCNC 440 file: 770 S3 0.75 kW, the 1100s 1.12 kW.\n- **Travel:** 770 S3 is 14 × 7.5 × 13.25 in. The 1100s are 18 × 9.5 × 16.5 in.\n- **Registration:** the files are registered in `MACHINES` (`crates/app/src/posting.rs`).\n- **Text-only edits:** the README's machine list, and the rigid-tap comment in `tormach.cps` (no output change).\n\n**Manual identification.** The decisions file records every figure with its manual, page and revision.\n- `pcnc1100-3-um-c4.1` is the **Series I** manual (C4-1, 2008). The Series II manual's revision history confirms this.\n- UM10087 1013A is the **Series 3** manual: its page footers read \"PCNC_1100_SERIES_3\".\n- The two 770 manuals differ only in the X/Y rapid: B1-4 (the pre-Series-3 770) gives 130 IPM and C1-1 (Series 3) gives 135. Only Series 3 got a file.\n\n**Still open on #170:** the PathPilot-era **1100M / 1100M+** that PathPilot Hub lists. We have no manual for them, so this PR says `Refs #170`.\n\n## Readings / tests\n- `tormach_machines` 5/5. Its manual-figures table now has 10 rows, and there are belt-note checks for the Series I ranges, the 1100s' 150 rpm low range and the 770 S3's 10100 rpm high range. All four new machines are covered by the rigid-tap refusal test.\n- `machine` 32/32, `tormach_post` 10/10, `posting` 17/17.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (upstream/main merged, clean): post, sim and app are green. The remaining reds also fail on upstream main: `swarf_pose_continuity` (fixed by #351) and the GPU headless tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\n**Not exercised:** a Hub simulation. PathPilot Hub has no simulator for these Mach3-era machines; the closest is the 770M. A GUI check of the machine list is pending with the contributor, so this stays a draft until that is done.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/170-tormach-pcnc.md`.\n\nChangelog: Machine files for the Tormach PCNC 770 (Series 3) and PCNC 1100 (Series I, II, 3), each from its operator's manual; these R8 mills refuse rigid taps by name (#170)\n\nRefs #170\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
